    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe change is coherent and mostly idiomatic \u2014 the Luhn logic moved cleanly out of `Owner.getCheckDigit()` into the controller's `luhnCheckDigit()` where the check digit is now minted at creation, `primaryIdentifier`/`OwnerCreatedEvent` were the single pivot point as their docstrings promised, and the segment-parsing readers (`getFiscalYear`, `getLocality`) were correctly flipped to read back from `memberId`. But one structural problem stands out:\n\n**`fiscalYearOf` is now duplicated verbatim across two units.**\n- `Owner.java:312` \u2014 `private static int fiscalYearOf(LocalDate date)` (still live; used by `getMembershipPoints()` for the tenure check at `Owner.java:360`).\n- `OwnerRestControllerV1.java:753` \u2014 a brand-new `private int fiscalYearOf(LocalDate date)` with byte-for-byte identical logic (`date.getMonthValue() >= 7 ? date.getYear() + 1 : date.getYear()`).\n\nThis change *introduced* the second copy: previously the controller's identity generation didn't need the fiscal year, so there was one definition; now both the model and the controller compute the same fiscal-year boundary independently. That's exactly the duplication this codebase already chose to avoid for the sibling derivation \u2014 the `HashUtils` docstring explicitly says the SHA-256 segment is shared \"rather than each copying the loop,\" and this diff even reuses `hashHex`/`HashUtils` for the HASH8 segment. The fiscal-year rule deserves the same treatment: a maintainer who later moves the FY boundary (or the \"year it ends in\" convention) must now find and sync two definitions, and the member id's baked-in FY and the model's tenure calculation can silently diverge.\n\nSuggested fix: extract the fiscal-year rule into one shared home (a small util alongside `HashUtils`, e.g. `FiscalYear.of(LocalDate)`, or a shared date-util method) and have both `Owner` and the controller call it, mirroring how HASH8 is shared. At minimum, don't leave two identical private `fiscalYearOf` methods in the model and the controller.\n\nMinor (not blocking on its own): `getFiscalYear()` and `getLocality()` both hardcode the fixed-suffix arithmetic (`length() - 11`, `- 9`, `< 12`) to slice FY/REGION out of the base. The magic `11` (= FY 2 + HASH8 8 + CHK 1) is repeated with slightly different guards in the two readers; a single named constant or a small `memberIdSegments()` helper would make the format contract one place rather than scattered offsets.",
